================================================================================================
V4 DIRECT READOUT — END-TO-END ACCURACY against V3's QPE sensing
================================================================================================
  6 PAIRED seeds, 20 epochs, k_steps=15, 8192 shots/circuit.
  Identical walk and schedule; the ONLY difference is the energy readout.

  problem                exact    V3 QPE  V4 direct     diff  sigma  V3 circ  V4 circ
  -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  H2                   -1.8573   -1.7563    -1.7522  +0.0041    0.6      160      240
  MaxCut N=4            0.0000    0.0422     0.0944  +0.0522    3.0      160      160
  Heisenberg N=4       -6.4641   -5.9942    -6.0175  -0.0233    1.7      160      320
  Heisenberg N=6       -9.9743   -8.9631    -8.9961  -0.0330    0.9      160      320

  diff = V4 - V3 on PAIRED seeds, so POSITIVE means V4 reached a higher
  (worse) energy. Sigma is on the paired difference. These notes record two
  sub-2-sigma results that reversed on replication, so read <2 sigma as a
  tie, not as a small effect.

  If V4 ties V3 here, the 2^N objection is answered empirically as well as
  by T2, and the billing projections in v21 stand. If V4 loses, the cheap
  variant is cheap because it does less, and v21's flat-in-N column is void.
